From: RD03v2 port maintainers
Subject: nss: an8855: switch the driver core from the Airoha special tag to tag_8021q

The NSS/PPE data plane cannot parse past the 4-byte Airoha special (MTK)
tag, so the NSS build tags DSA frames with a plain 802.1Q header instead
(DSA_TAG_PROTO_VSC73XX_8021Q) and lets the tag_8021q infrastructure carry
the source/dest port in the VID. This patch converts the driver core:

  - .get_tag_protocol reports VSC73XX_8021Q, and setup() registers the
    tag_8021q context (teardown unregisters it; .tag_8021q_vlan_add/_del
    program the VLAN table entries the tagger needs)
  - setup() CLEARS AN8855_PORT_SPEC_REPLACE_MODE|AN8855_PORT_SPEC_TAG on
    the CPU ports where the default build SETS them. This inversion is
    load-bearing in both directions: the default tagger needs the special
    tag on every CPU port, the 8021q tagger is destroyed by it.
  - user ports default to flood enabled (BCF/UNUF/UNMF/UNIPMF set): with
    tag_8021q the CPU TX path is a regular VLAN lookup, not the MTK
    forced-port path, so standalone ports must flood toward the CPU for
    host RX to work at all (issue #5 / 999-2760 shape)
  - fdb/mdb ops resolve the VID through an8855_fdb_vid() (standalone vs
    bridged keyspace, issue #7), and port_fdb_dump hides the tag_8021q
    VID range from userspace
  - CPU-port egress tagging is owned by setup() alone; the two writers of
    the PVID register pair (tag_8021q and the bridge) go through shadow
    PVIDs arbitrated by an8855_port_commit_vlan() (issue #11 / 999-2761)

This patch exists so files/ stays the ONLY source of an8855.c: it is the
former nss/overlay full-file fork expressed as a delta on top of
999-2757. Base-driver fixes now reach the NSS build automatically; if a
base change conflicts with this delta the build fails loudly here rather
than silently shipping a stale fork. See tools/check-nss-divergence.sh.

